1
00:02:31,069 --> 00:02:40,449
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:40,949 --> 00:02:44,769
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:46,129 --> 00:02:51,389
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:51,869 --> 00:02:57,969
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:57,969 --> 00:03:08,309
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:08,989 --> 00:03:12,229
I'm going to be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:15,749 --> 00:03:18,849
It's been two years since the War of the Best in Marineford.

8
00:03:19,289 --> 00:03:23,709
Scattered across the world, Luffy and his crew underwits special training to prepare for the trials ahead.

9
00:03:23,709 --> 00:03:29,849
Now, they return to the Saba Odi Archipelago and move forward to the next stage of their journey, the New World.

10
00:03:30,629 --> 00:03:32,969
Let nothing stop you from reaching the top!

11
00:03:35,129 --> 00:03:36,749
Listen up, guys!

12
00:03:37,449 --> 00:03:39,949
There's a lot I want to say, but we don't have much time.

13
00:03:40,229 --> 00:03:41,609
One thing can't wait, though.

14
00:03:42,029 --> 00:03:46,389
What you went through these past two years was selfish of me, so thanks for putting up with it.

15
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:49,729
Let's go!

16
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:49,849
Let's go!

17
00:03:49,849 --> 00:03:51,849
Let's go!

18
00:03:51,849 --> 00:04:02,049
The Man Who Guarded the Sunny

19
00:04:02,049 --> 00:04:07,629
Brother, it's too hard to dig here!

20
00:04:07,769 --> 00:04:08,849
Of course it is!

21
00:04:09,069 --> 00:04:11,329
This island is all rocks and tree roots.

22
00:04:12,329 --> 00:04:14,049
No, don't bury us!

23
00:04:14,109 --> 00:04:15,309
We're victims too!

24
00:04:15,449 --> 00:04:16,989
Please, I'll do anything you want!

25
00:04:17,049 --> 00:04:18,149
Just let me live!

26
00:04:18,149 --> 00:04:19,009
Captain Luffy!

27
00:04:19,009 --> 00:04:20,329
No, I mean Black!

28
00:04:20,429 --> 00:04:21,789
He made us do this!

29
00:04:23,109 --> 00:04:25,749
Listen, I have a secret to share with you.

30
00:04:26,649 --> 00:04:30,429
We didn't give a damn about going to the New World with the Straw Hats.

31
00:04:30,429 --> 00:04:39,909
The reason we joined was so we could stab them in the back and collect their bounties without

32
00:04:39,909 --> 00:04:41,669
them ever suspecting a thing.

33
00:04:43,969 --> 00:04:44,449
No!

34
00:04:44,829 --> 00:04:45,189
Drift!

35
00:04:45,449 --> 00:04:46,269
Stop it!

36
00:04:46,489 --> 00:04:50,389
I don't know what that goopy stuff is, but you're going to kill him if you keep that up!

37
00:04:50,429 --> 00:04:51,909
I won't let my friend die!

38
00:04:52,509 --> 00:04:53,209
Got him!

39
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:54,609
Take that, bastard!

40
00:04:58,789 --> 00:05:00,109
Uh-oh.

41
00:05:00,549 --> 00:05:01,489
That's weird.

42
00:05:01,989 --> 00:05:02,509
Whoa!

43
00:05:04,049 --> 00:05:09,609
And sure, your straw hat did look a little off, but it had been two years, so I didn't think

44
00:05:09,609 --> 00:05:10,449
much of it.

45
00:05:11,029 --> 00:05:16,929
You lied without remorse, and deception is a sin, one that you will be buried for.

46
00:05:16,929 --> 00:05:20,389
Brother, how goes the grave?

47
00:05:20,469 --> 00:05:21,049
I'm digging!

48
00:05:21,289 --> 00:05:21,809
I'm digging!

49
00:05:22,009 --> 00:05:24,369
Sinners all, these poor fools.

50
00:05:25,249 --> 00:05:26,189
Gods in heaven.

51
00:05:27,449 --> 00:05:29,209
Please, forgive them.

52
00:05:29,589 --> 00:05:31,189
Grant them peace and death.

53
00:05:31,429 --> 00:05:32,029
Yes!

54
00:05:32,389 --> 00:05:32,669
No!

55
00:05:33,129 --> 00:05:35,149
Peace, yes, but not death!

56
00:05:35,509 --> 00:05:38,469
Still, it's not all bad, I suppose.

57
00:05:39,129 --> 00:05:40,989
I did find the real Luffy.

58
00:05:41,529 --> 00:05:42,689
Hehehehehe!

59
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:45,889
I told you there wasn't any choice in the matter.

60
00:05:46,149 --> 00:05:47,209
What did you expect?

61
00:05:47,989 --> 00:05:49,529
Dark King Rayleigh was there.

62
00:05:49,869 --> 00:05:51,149
He's as strong as Kizalu.

63
00:05:51,609 --> 00:05:54,629
Even with the pacifistas, we couldn't so much as slow him down.

64
00:05:55,609 --> 00:05:59,169
Unfortunately, the Caribou Brothers escaped along with the rest of their crew.

65
00:05:59,569 --> 00:06:03,789
It seems they took some of the fake straw hats with them as well, though I can't imagine

66
00:06:03,789 --> 00:06:04,229
why.

67
00:06:04,329 --> 00:06:08,449
At any rate, we captured most of the pirates, even though the real straw hats heavily

68
00:06:08,449 --> 00:06:10,189
damaged two of our pacifistas.

69
00:06:10,769 --> 00:06:14,229
One of the units was the same prototype they fought before.

70
00:06:14,649 --> 00:06:17,109
Its strength hasn't changed in the last two years.

71
00:06:17,549 --> 00:06:19,509
That's bad news for us.

72
00:06:20,809 --> 00:06:25,169
I don't know what they've been up to, but the straw hats are immeasurably more dangerous

73
00:06:25,169 --> 00:06:25,889
than before.

74
00:06:26,729 --> 00:06:30,229
Tell the Marines in the New World that they have a new threat coming their way.

75
00:06:31,189 --> 00:06:34,869
The straw hats have returned, and they're stronger than we could have imagined.

76
00:06:38,449 --> 00:06:49,149
A pity they had to take off so soon.

77
00:06:53,769 --> 00:06:55,229
But I'm proud of them.

78
00:06:55,909 --> 00:06:56,549
They're tough.

79
00:06:56,789 --> 00:06:57,989
They're gonna do just fine.

80
00:06:59,269 --> 00:07:00,329
You were watching?

81
00:07:00,329 --> 00:07:01,209
Yes.

82
00:07:01,369 --> 00:07:02,209
I'm a big fan.

83
00:07:06,109 --> 00:07:07,829
I know that smile, Ray.

84
00:07:08,109 --> 00:07:09,309
What's on your mind?

85
00:07:10,009 --> 00:07:10,209
Huh?

86
00:07:11,029 --> 00:07:11,309
Ah.

87
00:07:12,829 --> 00:07:13,969
It's nothing, really.

88
00:07:13,969 --> 00:07:21,749
Whoa-ho-ho!

89
00:07:22,289 --> 00:07:22,769
Huh?

90
00:07:23,049 --> 00:07:25,049
Hey, that's a nice ship you got there.

91
00:07:25,129 --> 00:07:26,769
Thanks, but it's not exactly mine.

92
00:07:26,969 --> 00:07:29,229
Rather, I stole it after my house burned down.

93
00:07:29,529 --> 00:07:30,249
Oh, yeah?

94
00:07:30,549 --> 00:07:31,629
And what's your name?

95
00:07:31,829 --> 00:07:32,269
Rayleigh.

96
00:07:33,809 --> 00:07:35,029
My name's Roger.

97
00:07:35,489 --> 00:07:38,469
It's destiny meeting you, I say.

98
00:07:38,909 --> 00:07:39,509
Oh, yeah?

99
00:07:39,509 --> 00:07:43,809
How about we team up and turn this whole world upside down?

100
00:07:43,889 --> 00:07:44,109
Huh?

101
00:07:45,209 --> 00:07:47,049
And I thought I drank too much.

102
00:07:47,349 --> 00:07:50,829
I don't know who you are or what you're selling, but I'm not interested.

103
00:07:51,249 --> 00:07:53,069
Come on, you got a good thing going here.

104
00:07:53,309 --> 00:07:57,329
Your ship might be small, but if we handle it right, I bet it could even survive a storm.

105
00:07:57,709 --> 00:07:59,589
We could conquer the seas in this thing.

106
00:07:59,929 --> 00:08:00,829
Let's set sail!

107
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:02,229
What do you mean, we?

108
00:08:02,229 --> 00:08:04,309
I just met you half a minute ago.

109
00:08:04,669 --> 00:08:06,509
Why don't you get your own damn boat?

110
00:08:06,509 --> 00:08:12,269
One of these days, you're going to look back at this and realize it was the beginning of the greatest adventure ever known.

111
00:08:12,809 --> 00:08:24,009
Before then, I never believed much in fate, but maybe nothing really happens by accident.

112
00:08:25,189 --> 00:08:28,349
We're just too blind to see all the signs.

113
00:08:28,789 --> 00:08:31,969
Anyway, that hat found the right man.

114
00:08:31,969 --> 00:08:35,269
So long as it sails, I'll stay here, waiting.

115
00:08:36,249 --> 00:08:39,249
Because I want to see a new king before I die.

116
00:08:40,149 --> 00:08:42,909
The surface is already so far away.

117
00:08:43,309 --> 00:08:44,109
What a view!

118
00:08:44,449 --> 00:08:47,049
I've been under before, but portholes on a submarine?

119
00:08:47,349 --> 00:08:48,829
They got nothing on this!

120
00:08:49,189 --> 00:08:49,969
We're sinking!

121
00:08:50,609 --> 00:08:51,049
Sinking!

122
00:08:51,629 --> 00:08:52,609
What if we get a leak?

123
00:08:52,729 --> 00:08:53,969
This is freaking me out!

124
00:08:53,969 --> 00:08:57,149
Yeah, it feels like we're leaving the whole world behind.

125
00:08:57,549 --> 00:08:58,209
It's eerie.

126
00:08:58,549 --> 00:08:59,249
No big deal.

127
00:08:59,729 --> 00:09:01,869
I've done this like a bajillion times before.

128
00:09:02,249 --> 00:09:02,809
It's cool.

129
00:09:04,069 --> 00:09:06,429
Nope, not pooping my pants at all here.

130
00:09:08,609 --> 00:09:10,869
The ocean sure is awesome!

131
00:09:10,869 --> 00:09:20,249
Look at that!

132
00:09:20,349 --> 00:09:21,889
They really are trees, huh?

133
00:09:24,889 --> 00:09:27,269
Wow, I totally forgot about that!

134
00:09:29,649 --> 00:09:31,349
They're giant mangroves.

135
00:09:31,509 --> 00:09:35,829
You can't tell when you're up top, but it's sure quite a sight to see from down here.

136
00:09:35,989 --> 00:09:38,589
The majesty of nature is truly humbling!

137
00:09:38,589 --> 00:09:42,849
Why, my eyes would be popping out of my skull if I had any eyes to speak of, I mean.

138
00:09:44,069 --> 00:09:45,109
Who cares?

139
00:09:45,249 --> 00:09:46,069
I've seen this.

140
00:09:46,269 --> 00:09:47,829
Because you got on the wrong ship!

141
00:09:48,149 --> 00:09:48,909
Shut up!

142
00:09:49,069 --> 00:09:50,669
Don't ruin this for us!

143
00:09:51,089 --> 00:09:53,129
These roots, they're beautiful.

144
00:09:53,709 --> 00:09:54,629
And think about it.

145
00:09:55,229 --> 00:09:58,189
They stretch all the way down to the bottom of the sea.

146
00:10:04,469 --> 00:10:05,729
Okay, you win.

147
00:10:05,729 --> 00:10:09,689
Hey, Chopper, I think there's something behind that tree.

148
00:10:09,889 --> 00:10:10,229
Huh?

149
00:10:11,509 --> 00:10:12,149
Whoa!

150
00:10:12,529 --> 00:10:13,769
It's huge!

151
00:10:14,649 --> 00:10:16,389
Took us long enough to get here.

152
00:10:16,589 --> 00:10:18,269
But whatever, it was worth the wait.

153
00:10:18,569 --> 00:10:19,909
I wonder what comes next.

154
00:10:20,169 --> 00:10:21,249
Oh, fishies!

155
00:10:21,609 --> 00:10:21,829
Huh?

156
00:10:22,349 --> 00:10:23,629
Then I can grab them!

157
00:10:23,629 --> 00:10:25,389
I see.

158
00:10:25,689 --> 00:10:26,849
These look pretty good, too.

159
00:10:27,089 --> 00:10:27,709
Here goes.

160
00:10:29,409 --> 00:10:30,789
That's not funny!

161
00:10:31,369 --> 00:10:33,769
If you put that bubble in, we'll die!

162
00:10:34,029 --> 00:10:35,569
I'm gonna kill you!

163
00:10:35,909 --> 00:10:36,329
Twice!

164
00:10:36,429 --> 00:10:38,469
Nami, you know how the coding works, right?

165
00:10:38,649 --> 00:10:41,729
Can we get some basic tips before another idiot flips out on us?

166
00:10:41,989 --> 00:10:42,529
Good point.

167
00:10:42,929 --> 00:10:43,209
Okay.

168
00:10:43,769 --> 00:10:46,129
Rayleigh gave me a manual, but I can summarize it.

169
00:10:46,389 --> 00:10:48,129
So, listen closely, okay?

170
00:10:48,129 --> 00:10:49,429
She's real!

171
00:10:49,669 --> 00:10:51,029
I can die happy!

172
00:10:51,689 --> 00:10:52,529
Saatchi!

173
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:55,269
You don't have to take us with you!

174
00:10:55,369 --> 00:10:57,009
Who's flipping out now, idiot?

175
00:10:58,969 --> 00:10:59,529
What?

176
00:11:00,529 --> 00:11:02,509
His nosebleed shot out!

177
00:11:02,729 --> 00:11:03,229
I see.

178
00:11:03,649 --> 00:11:05,149
It maintains its shape well.

179
00:11:05,489 --> 00:11:06,729
You'd think that it would burst,

180
00:11:06,989 --> 00:11:11,089
especially considering the immense amount of water pressure the coding must be exposed to.

181
00:11:11,709 --> 00:11:12,389
How nice.

182
00:11:12,589 --> 00:11:15,649
And I thought we'd all drown down here, never to be seen again.

183
00:11:17,069 --> 00:11:17,669
Saatchi!

184
00:11:18,189 --> 00:11:19,449
Get out of the ocean!

185
00:11:21,449 --> 00:11:22,949
Bright seawater!

186
00:11:23,269 --> 00:11:24,069
Damn it!

187
00:11:24,369 --> 00:11:25,169
Keep pulling!

188
00:11:37,949 --> 00:11:38,549
Saatchi!

189
00:11:38,709 --> 00:11:40,389
What the heck happened to you back there?

190
00:11:40,629 --> 00:11:43,869
I knew you were weak to pretty girls, but this is a real liability!

191
00:11:44,189 --> 00:11:45,509
You're supposed to be cool!

192
00:11:45,969 --> 00:11:47,129
That poor man.

193
00:11:47,129 --> 00:11:51,129
I can only imagine the horrors he must have endured during the past two years.

194
00:11:51,769 --> 00:11:55,509
Let's hope he lives long enough to see the mermaids he was so looking forward to.

195
00:11:56,509 --> 00:12:01,309
And let's also hope they aren't quite so lovely that the sight of them strikes him dead.

196
00:12:01,309 --> 00:12:06,509
When we get there, we'll have to ask for blood donations, but they won't be human.

197
00:12:06,509 --> 00:12:09,149
I hope fishmen have the same kind of blood as him.

198
00:12:09,149 --> 00:12:18,329
So, Sunny's coding has the same properties as the bubbles on Saba-Odi, meaning that objects or people can pass in and out without causing it any harm at all.

199
00:12:18,329 --> 00:12:19,329
Spare me the bubble science!

200
00:12:19,329 --> 00:12:20,329
Spare me the bubble science!

201
00:12:20,329 --> 00:12:21,329
We got a man down here!

202
00:12:21,329 --> 00:12:23,329
Sanji aside, she's not wrong.

203
00:12:23,329 --> 00:12:25,709
We saw this all over Saba-Odi.

204
00:12:25,709 --> 00:12:29,709
It only stretches so far, then allows an object to pass through.

205
00:12:29,709 --> 00:12:38,089
So, the good news is, if we get attacked by any nasty sea creatures, we can still fire cannons at them, just like we would if we were above water.

206
00:12:38,089 --> 00:12:39,089
Huh?

207
00:12:39,089 --> 00:12:42,929
Wait, so what would pop it? Is it that durable?

208
00:12:42,929 --> 00:12:47,269
It does fine with single objects, but if too many things pass through at once, then it'll break.

209
00:12:47,269 --> 00:12:51,969
Let's see, like if a sea king clamps down on the ship, for example. That's bad.

210
00:12:51,969 --> 00:13:00,969
We're safe. Good riddance.

211
00:13:00,969 --> 00:13:04,409
Also, the coating doesn't protect the ship from anything except water.

212
00:13:04,409 --> 00:13:09,909
So, if we crash into a rock or a trench and the mast breaks or something like that, then the bubble could also burst.

213
00:13:09,909 --> 00:13:12,289
So, it's not like we can just bounce around down here.

214
00:13:12,289 --> 00:13:15,789
Still, as long as we take the usual precautions, we should be fine.

215
00:13:15,789 --> 00:13:19,029
I mean, I'm sure Luffy will try to get us all killed, but what else is new?

216
00:13:19,029 --> 00:13:22,289
So, we're in the clear after all. Good!

217
00:13:22,289 --> 00:13:31,169
Well, in theory at least, but a lot of ships try to make the trip to Fishman Island, and over 70% of them sink.

218
00:13:31,169 --> 00:13:34,669
We are so dead!

219
00:13:34,669 --> 00:13:39,669
One gum gum gatling, and I bet I can catch all the fish swimming out there.

220
00:13:39,669 --> 00:13:43,049
Yeah, if I cut enough holes in this bubble thing, I bet I could catch even more.

221
00:13:43,049 --> 00:13:46,049
Aren't you listening to Nami?

222
00:13:46,049 --> 00:13:50,049
That's too many holes! Our chances down here are bad enough as it is!

223
00:13:50,049 --> 00:13:52,929
Oh, break your bones! Let's fix them! Let's break them again!

224
00:13:52,929 --> 00:14:00,929
No fair! Haji said he'd show us the Fishman Island like it was no big deal, and now we're stuck in this death bubble slowly descending to our demise!

225
00:14:00,929 --> 00:14:08,269
Oh, yeah! Lunchtime! They packed a bunch of food for me! Since Sanji's sick, we should have ourselves a Pikmin!

226
00:14:08,269 --> 00:14:10,809
Yay! All that screaming made me hungry!

227
00:14:10,809 --> 00:14:20,809
And I'm wasting away! Cool! As long as Nami thinks the ship will stay stable. We don't have to steer it or anything right now, do we?

228
00:14:20,809 --> 00:14:31,809
Nope. We'll just be cruising on the sea current till we get further down. So, yeah. I'm sure we'll have more excitement a bit later, but for the time being, we might as well just kick back and take it easy.

229
00:14:31,809 --> 00:14:38,809
Well, I wouldn't call this taking it easy exactly, but there's something you guys should probably know before we reach Fishman Island.

230
00:15:01,809 --> 00:15:08,809
Now, this is a little heavy, so I hope it doesn't ruin lunch for everybody.

231
00:15:21,809 --> 00:15:24,809
I think I know. I'm ready.

232
00:15:24,809 --> 00:15:31,809
It's robot stuff, Bryce! You've got all kinds of secrets, don't you?

233
00:15:31,809 --> 00:15:34,809
Can you transform into a tank? Or wait, maybe?

234
00:15:34,809 --> 00:15:35,809
You've got laser guns!

235
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:37,809
Tell us, Robo-Bro!

236
00:15:37,809 --> 00:15:40,809
Super armored!

237
00:15:40,809 --> 00:15:41,809
Me.

238
00:15:46,809 --> 00:15:51,809
Sorry, no new secrets. Secrets inaccessible, Robo.

239
00:15:51,809 --> 00:15:53,809
He speaks robot!

240
00:15:53,809 --> 00:16:00,809
Okay, I know robots are cool, but listen up. Or eat and listen if you like.

241
00:16:04,809 --> 00:16:11,809
Like Usopp said, Hachi was supposed to show us the way to Fishman Island himself, but he got hurt real bad back on Saba Odi.

242
00:16:11,809 --> 00:16:14,809
He came down here ahead of us to get medical treatment.

243
00:16:14,809 --> 00:16:17,809
Anyway, it was the same thing that happened to Duval.

244
00:16:17,809 --> 00:16:22,809
Meaning, he was protecting the Sunny from anyone who came for it.

245
00:16:22,809 --> 00:16:27,809
Things got ugly about a year ago when the Navy found out the ship was docked there.

246
00:16:27,809 --> 00:16:30,809
Both him and Duval got taken out in a big fight.

247
00:16:30,809 --> 00:16:36,809
Huh? Wait, a year? Then who was protecting the Sunny after that?

248
00:16:36,809 --> 00:16:39,809
We had one more secret ally.

249
00:16:39,809 --> 00:16:41,809
If not really, then who?

250
00:16:41,809 --> 00:16:47,809
Someone who separated us two years ago, for better or worse. The Warlord.

251
00:16:47,809 --> 00:16:48,809
Huh?

252
00:16:49,809 --> 00:16:53,809
Turns out Bartholomew Kuma was on our side the whole time.

253
00:16:53,809 --> 00:16:58,809
A few days back, when I made it to the Sunny, I couldn't believe my eyes.

254
00:16:58,809 --> 00:17:00,809
He was right there.

255
00:17:05,809 --> 00:17:07,809
I've been waiting for you.

256
00:17:08,809 --> 00:17:10,809
What the hell are you doing here?

257
00:17:11,809 --> 00:17:13,809
Mission accomplished.

258
00:17:13,809 --> 00:17:34,809
You saw for yourself. There wasn't a single scratch on the Sunny.

259
00:17:34,809 --> 00:17:37,809
Later, Rayleigh gave me the whole story.

260
00:17:37,809 --> 00:17:40,809
I am a member of the Revolutionary Army.

261
00:17:40,809 --> 00:17:44,809
If it's within my power, I want to help the Straw Hats escape from here.

262
00:17:44,809 --> 00:17:48,809
You guys probably knew that something was up, but now we know the truth.

263
00:17:48,809 --> 00:17:51,809
He saved the Sunny, and he saved our lives.

264
00:17:53,809 --> 00:17:56,809
And then, after we were sent flying from the island,

265
00:17:56,809 --> 00:18:00,809
Kuma paid Rayleigh a visit and dropped another bombshell.

266
00:18:00,809 --> 00:18:04,809
I don't have much time. Not as myself.

267
00:18:04,809 --> 00:18:11,809
The details are a little sketchy, but evidently, Kuma surrendered his body to the Navy.

268
00:18:11,809 --> 00:18:15,809
They used him as an experiment and replaced his body parts one by one.

269
00:18:15,809 --> 00:18:20,809
By the time the War of the Best rolled around, his personality had been completely erased.

270
00:18:20,809 --> 00:18:26,809
Wait. He knew where he sent us, but he didn't know what we'd do once we got there, or that we would even make it back.

271
00:18:26,809 --> 00:18:31,809
And you said his personality was taken away, but he still protected the Sunny?

272
00:18:31,809 --> 00:18:37,809
The guy who worked on him is this dude named Dr. Vegapunk, and Kuma must have made a deal with him,

273
00:18:37,809 --> 00:18:40,809
because he programmed one final mission into his brain.

274
00:18:40,809 --> 00:18:46,809
Defend the Thousand Sunny from any attackers until the moment that a Straw Hat returns to claim it.

275
00:18:46,809 --> 00:18:50,809
So even though he's been reduced to a living weapon with no memory,

276
00:18:50,809 --> 00:18:57,809
he's been carrying out his own orders, protecting our ship for the past two years to fulfill his last wish.

277
00:18:57,809 --> 00:19:02,809
But why? He barely knew us. I mean, why'd it matter to him?

278
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:05,809
I don't know. Maybe it's cause of Luffy.

279
00:19:05,809 --> 00:19:10,809
You said Kuma was part of the Revolutionary Army, and Luffy's dad was the leader of those guys, right?

280
00:19:10,809 --> 00:19:15,809
I don't know much about my dad, but it seems like that robot bear dude was a good guy,

281
00:19:15,809 --> 00:19:18,809
so we can't be too bad if they're friends.

282
00:19:18,809 --> 00:19:19,809
Kuma...

283
00:19:19,809 --> 00:19:25,809
The bottom line is, our survival and all the things we accomplished in the past two years we owe to him.

284
00:19:25,809 --> 00:19:28,809
Whatever his reason was, we should be grateful.

285
00:19:28,809 --> 00:19:34,809
And we may never find out the truth, because it's not like we can ask him to explain himself anymore.

286
00:19:34,809 --> 00:19:40,809
All we can do now is honor his memory, and know that Bartholomew Kuma was our greatest ally,

287
00:19:40,809 --> 00:19:43,809
until he took his last breath as a human.

288
00:19:43,809 --> 00:19:50,809
Unfortunately, we'll never be able to thank him, since he'll just be a weapon, and likely our enemy the next time we meet.

289
00:19:50,809 --> 00:19:52,809
That's all I wanted to say.

290
00:19:52,809 --> 00:19:58,809
Kind of a lot to work through all at once, isn't it? Someday. I hope we can at least find out the rest of the story.

291
00:19:58,809 --> 00:20:00,809
Kuma saved us, huh?

292
00:20:00,809 --> 00:20:01,809
Oh, you're awake. Good.

293
00:20:01,809 --> 00:20:04,809
Have some lunch! It's from Amazon Lily.

294
00:20:04,809 --> 00:20:07,809
Oh, Amazon Lily. The island with all the women.

295
00:20:07,809 --> 00:20:11,809
Of course that's where he sent you. Do you know where I was these past two years?

296
00:20:11,809 --> 00:20:17,809
Because I'm kinda thinking Kuma's not such a good friend after all. In fact, if he were here right now, I'd like to kick his metal face in!

297
00:20:17,809 --> 00:20:26,809
Now, now, Sanji. We've all had our share of troubles. Before I became a pop music sensation, I was trapped in a cage. Still, the only thing that matters now is the voyage awaiting us.

298
00:20:26,809 --> 00:20:28,809
You don't know, man! You don't know anything!

299
00:20:28,809 --> 00:20:32,809
Straight ahead! Brother! Look! It's them!

300
00:20:32,809 --> 00:20:41,809
I know! Like you said, they're straight ahead. You think I'm blind? Looks like we'll be sailing with the Straw Hats after all.

301
00:20:41,809 --> 00:20:43,809
Well, how far down are we?

302
00:20:43,809 --> 00:20:47,809
I don't know, but it's getting darker and darker.

303
00:20:47,809 --> 00:20:55,809
We passed the photic zone, and it looks like we're around the bottom of the aphotic zone. About a thousand meters, give or take.

304
00:20:55,809 --> 00:21:03,809
It's quiet, and the sunny itself feels oddly still. It's almost like floating in the sky.

305
00:21:03,809 --> 00:21:08,809
The sky. I learned so much about weather up there, but I don't know if it's much use under water.

306
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:10,809
Hey, look! It's a whale!

307
00:21:10,809 --> 00:21:12,809
It's just like Laboon!

308
00:21:12,809 --> 00:21:15,809
Nah, it looks more like Whitebeard.

309
00:21:15,809 --> 00:21:28,809
I can't think about whales right now. I can't think about anything except the fact that I'm going to die. Or at least 70% going to die.

310
00:21:28,809 --> 00:21:33,809
Why did they tell me that? Maybe if I keep a lookout, I can raise our chances of making it out of this.

311
00:21:33,809 --> 00:21:41,809
Better than just sitting here. I don't see any big scary sea kings or stuff the ship could crash into. So I guess we're good for now.

312
00:21:41,809 --> 00:21:47,809
Wait a sec. What is that thing? A fish? No.

313
00:21:47,809 --> 00:21:50,809
Are you ready? We only get one shot at this!

314
00:21:50,809 --> 00:21:52,809
Ready, brother!

315
00:21:52,809 --> 00:21:53,809
Ready, Captain!

316
00:21:53,809 --> 00:21:56,809
Before you say anything, I know what you're thinking.

317
00:21:56,809 --> 00:21:58,809
Just shoot them, and they'll all drown.

318
00:21:58,809 --> 00:22:02,809
They're wanted dead or alive after all, so why not let them die?

319
00:22:02,809 --> 00:22:07,809
Well, that wouldn't do at all, because the Navy wouldn't know who killed them.

320
00:22:07,809 --> 00:22:12,809
We have to deliver their heads personally on a silver platter. Then they will fear us!

321
00:22:12,809 --> 00:22:16,809
The whole world will know our strength!

322
00:22:16,809 --> 00:22:19,809
We'll take them out before they suspect a thing!

323
00:22:19,809 --> 00:22:23,809
My big smiling face is the last thing they'll see before they die!

324
00:22:23,809 --> 00:22:26,809
Yes, sir! Uh, right, yeah!

325
00:22:26,809 --> 00:22:31,809
Hey, you guys, there's a ship-looking thing coming our way!

326
00:22:31,809 --> 00:22:32,809
What?

327
00:22:32,809 --> 00:22:33,809
You sure?

328
00:22:33,809 --> 00:22:35,809
Why don't you come look for yourself?

329
00:22:35,809 --> 00:22:36,809
Charge!

330
00:22:44,809 --> 00:22:45,809
It's a pirate ship!

331
00:22:45,809 --> 00:22:47,809
They're ramming straight into us!

332
00:22:47,809 --> 00:22:51,809
Go away, you morons! You're gonna make us all drown!

333
00:22:51,809 --> 00:23:01,809
They're not trying to break our ship! They're trying to board it!

334
00:23:01,809 --> 00:23:03,809
Damn it! Who are they?

335
00:23:03,809 --> 00:23:13,809
The Suni continues descending towards Fishman Island now with a decidedly unwelcome caribou on board.

336
00:23:13,809 --> 00:23:21,809
With their bubble threatening to pop at every turn, the crew braves an undersea waterfall only to stumble into the den of the legendary monster, the Kraken.

337
00:23:21,809 --> 00:23:26,809
With no way to battle such a massive foe, a watery grave seems all but inevitable.

338
00:23:26,809 --> 00:23:32,809
On the next One Piece, deadly combat under the sea, the demon of the ocean strikes!

339
00:23:32,809 --> 00:23:34,809
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

